## GenAI Migration: providers/gemini.py (Core Chat)

> **Date:** 2026-01-08
> **Status:** ✅ Complete with Dual-Engine Fallback

Refactored the core chat engine to use the modern [DualEngineLLM](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/llm_client.py#13-212) abstraction while preserving critical legacy functionality.

### Key Implementation Details

1.  **Dual-Engine Injection:** Replaced direct `genai.GenerativeModel` usage with [DualEngineLLM](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/llm_client.py#13-212).
2.  **Key Rotation Preserved:** Maintained sophisticated round-robin key management by injecting specific keys into the adapter per request.
3.  **Robust Legacy Fallback:**
    -   Detected that `google-generativeai` (legacy SDK) requires tools to be initialized in the constructor (unlike newer versions/docs).
    -   Patched [llm_client.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/llm_client.py) to support this by re-instantiating a temporary model when tools are detected.
    -   Fixed `system_instruction` compatibility issue with older legacy SDKs.
4.  **Verification:**
    -   Automated script ([verify_gemini_refactor.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/scripts/verify_gemini_refactor.py)) confirmed:
        -   ✅ Chat: Works (uses default engine logic).
        -   ✅ Tools: Works (forces Legacy engine + re-instantiates model).

